  "problem": "Let $f(x)$ be the $2L$-periodic extension of a function $F(x)$ from $x\\in [-L,L)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)\u223c\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061({{field-1}})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061({{field-2}}).\n$$\n\nThe $2$nd cosine coefficient of the series is\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $F(x)=\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({x}^{2}+1)$ and $L=3,$ the $2$nd cosine coefficient becomes\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}={{field-4}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-5}}.\n$$",
